# Build context exclusions for workloads/docker/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile's `COPY . .` takes the repository root as its context. Without
# this file that context was 6.2 GB — 5.7 GB of it `.worktrees/` — and a build
# filled the disk before it could commit a layer. It also copied real provider
# credentials into an image layer, where they persist even if a later stage
# removes them.

# Working trees for topic desks: gitignored, each carrying its own node_modules.
.worktrees/

# Dependencies are installed inside the image from the copied manifests; a host
# install is the wrong libc anyway (host glibc, image alpine/musl).
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Credentials. `packages/tech/.env` holds live provider API keys — an image layer
# is not a place to put them, and nothing in the image needs them at build time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.worktree

# Version-control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore

# Build output and caches — regenerated inside the image when needed.
docs/.vitepress/cache/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
**/dist/
**/.cache/
*.log

# Local scratch that has no meaning inside a container.
.claude/
